  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nDry conditions will persist through the weekend until our next \nfront. Our next cold front is expected to swing through early next \nweek in association with a potent low that will progress through the \nsouthern Great Plains. There is still some disagreements on a few \nthings such as timing and the extent of the associated front south. \nThough as it sits this will likely be our next chance for some \nactivity. We'll be able to get a better grasp on things when we get \nin the range of the CAMs. Therefore be sure check back for future \nupdates. \n\nFor Halloween locations will remain dry. Not only are we expected to \nbe dry, but low temperatures will stay in the 70s/upper 60s with \nlight winds Halloween night.\n\nWill have to continue to monitor the possibility for minor coastal \nflooding along Gulf facing beaches into the weekend. This will be \ndue to persistent onshore flow and elevated swell periods. An \nincreased risk of rip currents will also persist.",
